---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, DATA_PATHS, href } from '../data/site';

const lastUpdated = 'October 12, 2026';
const toc = [
  ['meta-compliance', 'Statement'],
  ['disconnect', '1. Disconnect an account'],
  ['delete-profile', '2. Delete a profile'],
  ['delete-everything', '3. Remove everything'],
  ['revoke', '4. Revoke from the platform'],
  ['confirmation', 'Confirmation'],
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`User Data Deletion Instructions: ${SITE.fullName}`}
  description="How to delete every piece of data Reelay holds about your Instagram, Facebook, Threads, YouTube, TikTok and Bluesky accounts. It is all on your own computer, and removing it takes effect immediately."
>
  <header class="doc-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1>User Data Deletion</h1>
      <p class="lede">Everything Reelay keeps about your accounts is on your own computer, so you can delete it yourself, at once. <strong>Here is how, step by step.</strong></p>
      <p class="doc-meta">Last updated {lastUpdated} · For Meta Platform Terms and Google API Services User Data Policy</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap doc-layout">
    <nav class="doc-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <div>
        <p>On this page</p>
        <ol>{toc.map(([id, label]) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a></li>)}</ol>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <div class="legal-content">
      <section id="meta-compliance" class="doc-summary">
        <h2>Data deletion statement</h2>
        <p class="statement">Reelay does not store your social account data on cloud servers. Your account tokens are kept in your computer’s keychain, and your drafts and account details in Reelay’s database on your computer. To delete them, click <strong>Disconnect</strong> on the account under <strong>Accounts</strong> in Reelay, or delete the Reelay data folder at <code>{DATA_PATHS.mac}</code> (Mac) or <code>{DATA_PATHS.windows}</code> (Windows).</p>
      </section>

      <section id="disconnect">
        <h2>1. Disconnect an account</h2>
        <p>The quickest way to remove one platform account (Instagram, Facebook Page, Threads, YouTube, TikTok or Bluesky):</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Open Reelay and click <strong>Accounts</strong> in the sidebar.</li>
          <li>Find the account’s card and click <strong>Disconnect</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>What happens straight away:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Reelay asks the platform to revoke the access token where it can: Google’s revocation endpoint for YouTube, and the platform’s own revocation for accounts you signed in to with Reelay’s app.</li>
          <li>The token is deleted from the macOS Keychain or Windows Credential Manager.</li>
          <li>The account (its name, ID and picture) is removed from Reelay’s database.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If the same account is connected to another profile, it stays connected there until you disconnect it there too. Videos and tickets you made stay on your computer until you delete them with method 2 or 3.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="delete-profile">
        <h2>2. Delete a profile</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>Click the profile at the top of the sidebar, or open the <strong>Profile</strong> menu.</li>
          <li>Choose <strong>Delete Profile…</strong> and confirm.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>The profile’s board, tickets, drafts and connected accounts are removed from Reelay, and each account is disconnected as in method 1. Downloaded video files stay in the profile’s library folder for you to keep or delete. Delete Profile is available when you have more than one profile; with only one, use method 3.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="delete-everything">
        <h2>3. Remove everything</h2>
        <p>Quit Reelay, then delete its data folder. This removes the database (<code>{DATA_PATHS.dbName}</code>) with every profile, ticket, transcript, rule and history entry, plus Reelay’s caches.</p>
        <h3>Mac</h3>
        <pre><code>rm -rf ~/Library/Application\ Support/Reelay ~/Library/Logs/Reelay</code></pre>
        <p>Or in Finder: press <code>⌘⇧G</code>, paste <code>{DATA_PATHS.mac}</code>, and move the folder to the Trash.</p>
        <h3>Windows</h3>
        <pre><code>Remove-Item -Recurse -Force "{DATA_PATHS.windowsPs}", "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\Reelay"</code></pre>
        <p>Or in File Explorer: go to <code>{DATA_PATHS.windows}</code> and delete the folder.</p>
        <h3>Then</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Sign-ins:</strong> delete the entries named <strong>Reelay</strong> in Keychain Access (Mac) or Credential Manager → Windows Credentials (Windows).</li>
          <li><strong>A shared database:</strong> if you moved the database to Google Drive, Dropbox, iCloud Drive or OneDrive, delete <code>{DATA_PATHS.dbName}</code> from that folder too.</li>
          <li><strong>Videos:</strong> delete your library folder (by default <code>~/Movies/Reelay</code> or <code>Videos\Reelay</code>) if you don’t want to keep the files.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="revoke">
        <h2>4. Revoke Reelay from the platform</h2>
        <p>You can also remove Reelay’s access from the platform itself at any time, even if Reelay is no longer installed:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Facebook and Instagram:</strong> Facebook <a href="https://www.facebook.com/settings?tab=business_tools" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Settings &amp; privacy → Business integrations</a> (or Apps and websites), find Reelay and choose Remove.</li>
          <li><strong>Threads:</strong> in Threads, Settings → Account → Website permissions, then remove Reelay.</li>
          <li><strong>Google and YouTube:</strong> <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Account → Third-party apps and services</a>, select Reelay and choose Delete all connections.</li>
          <li><strong>TikTok:</strong> in TikTok, Settings and privacy → Security and permissions → Apps and services permissions, then remove Reelay.</li>
          <li><strong>Bluesky:</strong> Settings → Privacy and security → App passwords, then delete the password you made for Reelay.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="confirmation">
        <h2>Confirmation</h2>
        <p>Deletion on your computer takes effect immediately; there is no waiting period. Reelay has no server copy of your account data to delete. Its sign-in server keeps nothing once a sign-in is finished (see the <a href={`${href('/privacy')}#sign-in-server`}>Privacy Policy</a>).</p>
        <p>If you need written confirmation for a request, or help with any of these steps, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.complianceEmail}`}>{SITE.complianceEmail}</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .statement { color: var(--r-ink); font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.6; }
</style>
